Yeah. Can we talk about this real quick?

00:26:55.120 --> 00:26:56.740
Like just in general, in every.

00:26:57.280 --> 00:26:59.980
Airport security was a lot more lax back in the 80s.

00:26:59.980 --> 00:27:06.620
In every level, there are just, they're animated in the same way that an enemy might pop out

00:27:06.620 --> 00:27:12.020
of cover. And I get that they had to have different obstacles or different things you couldn't shoot.

00:27:12.180 --> 00:27:17.580
But every time it happened, I'm just like thinking, oh, it's like, oh, what's that noise?

00:27:17.580 --> 00:27:21.040
And looking and staring at you and then coming back around.

00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:24.720
And then, yeah, the kid skateboarding through a gunfight.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.880
Right. Like where are the caution codes?

00:27:27.280 --> 00:27:28.580
Why is nobody stopping you?

00:27:28.580 --> 00:27:31.500
The ones that are on the plane, like they know that they're being hijacked.

00:27:31.580 --> 00:27:32.760
They just stick their head out of the window.

00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:36.260
Well, Maya and I open the emergency exit and see what's happening.

00:27:36.460 --> 00:27:40.240
And then. Well, I prefer to think that in that situation, the terrorists are using them.

00:27:40.420 --> 00:27:42.060
I'm like. Well, sometimes they are.

00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:44.720
They are illustrated as being hostages.

00:27:44.720 --> 00:27:47.120
But sometimes it's just people checking out.

00:27:48.120 --> 00:27:51.060
There's one lady in purple and she looks like she's like a cane or something.

00:27:51.200 --> 00:27:52.520
And she like stomps her foot down.

00:27:52.660 --> 00:27:54.440
And like, I'm going to look here right now.

00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:55.540
And like for a long time.

00:27:55.540 --> 00:28:02.560
There's also the one that I think Sam was talking about, the bathing beauty, as she described.

00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:07.260
She comes out behind a tree and she's just wearing a bikini.

00:28:07.560 --> 00:28:10.220
And first off, it's like it was never implied that we were at the beach.

00:28:10.680 --> 00:28:12.460
So what are you doing wearing a bikini?

00:28:12.620 --> 00:28:14.420
But also, she's immune to bullets.

00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:15.920
Yeah. So she's got nothing to worry about.

00:28:15.940 --> 00:28:16.840
She's got a superpower.

00:28:17.040 --> 00:28:19.320
What is she not doing taking care of the terrorists?

00:28:19.320 --> 00:28:20.500
Well, hold on.

00:28:20.640 --> 00:28:22.180
I guess I don't remember.

00:28:22.340 --> 00:28:28.500
But if you shoot other bystanders, do they register?

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:32.040
Yeah. They are. That's what gets your error count.

00:28:32.100 --> 00:28:34.840
Okay. Yeah. You're right. They get the same blood splat and everything.

00:28:35.140 --> 00:28:38.560
I guess. I thought maybe just the error count went up, but they didn't animate anything.

00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:43.000
Nobody wants to see a bathing beauty die, regardless of the video game or real life.

00:28:43.020 --> 00:28:46.960
I just think it's weird. I mean, if they're using it as a distraction, then I don't know.

00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:47.860
They should go.

00:28:48.180 --> 00:28:53.440
Yeah. But I think it's something about the fact that they're not covered by clothing that would

00:28:53.440 --> 00:28:55.620
make it unfortunate if you shot them.

00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:57.220
Yeah. That's it.

00:28:57.580 --> 00:28:59.780
That's got to be what it is, because I can't think of anything else.

00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:01.300
Did it get harder?

00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:03.340
Yeah, I think so. I think it did.

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:09.340
Yeah. I think not only did it get harder, but I was running into a constant problem of not

00:29:09.860 --> 00:29:15.280
being able to heal, and therefore just an endurance run to see if I could get to scene

00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:16.300
three, maybe. Yeah.

00:29:16.760 --> 00:29:19.160
You know? I did get pretty far.

00:29:19.280 --> 00:29:21.300
I never got to the hideout.

00:29:21.300 --> 00:29:23.440
But I think that...

00:29:23.440 --> 00:29:30.360
I know. I think that there just needed to be something in this game to help people who wanted to play

00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:31.820
through it, because it's pretty engaging.

00:29:32.260 --> 00:29:34.160
There needed to be something there for those people.

00:29:34.220 --> 00:29:36.640
What do you mean? Who wanted to play through the entirety of the game.

00:29:36.720 --> 00:29:37.700
He wants it to be...

00:29:37.700 --> 00:29:38.620
Difficulty mode or something.

00:29:38.920 --> 00:29:40.000
Oh, you mean something harder?

00:29:40.300 --> 00:29:43.180
Not like... I'm not trying to play a story mode, so I don't need to be invincible.

00:29:43.180 --> 00:29:46.560
But I know I meant like there should have been something where it's like, oh, this is the

00:29:46.560 --> 00:29:49.560
easy mode, and you do heal between scenes or something like that.

00:29:49.820 --> 00:29:53.560
Something other than just like, the only way you're ever going to make it through is if

00:29:53.560 --> 00:29:58.220
you can shoot everybody in .05 seconds when they show up.

00:29:58.220 --> 00:29:59.880
These guys shoot very fast.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.160
Much faster than any zapper game we've seen.

00:30:02.580 --> 00:30:04.760
I do feel like as I played, I got better.

00:30:04.940 --> 00:30:06.020
I never got to level 5.

00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:07.800
We were stuck on level 4.

00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:13.700
But I feel like if I played a lot longer, I could maybe get to level 5 the way it is.

00:30:13.800 --> 00:30:17.220
And there were times, I don't know why, there were times that I didn't hit the health thing.

00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:18.160
I've never hit the health thing.

00:30:18.220 --> 00:30:20.300
But there were times where I would just regain all my health.

00:30:20.560 --> 00:30:21.460
I don't know if there's something that happened.

00:30:21.460 --> 00:30:22.640
I think it's a point 20 thing.

00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:26.040
So that made it, on those times, that definitely made it a lot easier.

00:30:26.040 --> 00:30:29.940
I just think, if we're thinking about the other zapper games we've played, I'm even thinking

00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:31.600
about Wild Gunman specifically.

00:30:32.400 --> 00:30:36.740
That one, even in the one-on-one dueling shootout, never gave me a problem.

00:30:36.980 --> 00:30:38.140
We played that one together.

00:30:38.320 --> 00:30:41.240
And it was always like, you could always shoot faster than them.

00:30:41.600 --> 00:30:42.980
Yeah, but it's not as fun.

00:30:43.020 --> 00:30:49.560
No, it's not fun. But I'm saying this one was incredibly, almost from the get-go, you had to be reactive.

00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:52.300
You had to have your gun ready on any particular person.

00:30:52.300 --> 00:30:57.280
Whereas in Hogan's Alley, which is a similar game with a test of like, will you shoot the

00:30:57.640 --> 00:30:58.760
bad guy or the cop?

00:30:59.200 --> 00:31:00.260
That was a test one too.

00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:01.740
And even that one gave you more time.

00:31:01.880 --> 00:31:03.060
I just think I need a little more time.

00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:06.860
I feel like towards the end, the timing was tough.

00:31:07.020 --> 00:31:09.980
But I just felt like once you got the hang of it, it wasn't the...

00:31:10.340 --> 00:31:13.980
I guess it was the time combined with the amount of things that were on the screen that

00:31:13.980 --> 00:31:14.820
started making it hard.

00:31:15.060 --> 00:31:19.080
But I feel like if we had too much more time, you would rarely get hit.

00:31:20.080 --> 00:31:22.860
I guess, yeah, I guess it's just a...

00:31:23.700 --> 00:31:24.860
It's completely subjective.

00:31:25.300 --> 00:31:31.020
Yeah. It's objectively difficult, but whether that's annoying to you or not...

00:31:31.020 --> 00:31:33.940
Yeah, I mean, it definitely could have been a little easier and still been difficult.

00:31:34.180 --> 00:31:36.140
Yeah. But the difficulty didn't like...

00:31:36.140 --> 00:31:39.740
It didn't feel like Ghost and Goblin's difficulty to me or anything.

00:31:39.860 --> 00:31:40.840
Maybe you should just play with a friend.

00:31:41.560 --> 00:31:42.760
Maybe that's what I should have done.

00:31:43.240 --> 00:31:45.220
Because, yeah, did any of us play a two-player?

00:31:45.340 --> 00:31:50.400
You did. Yeah, I played with Mark, who everybody knows now is the phantom other player that I frequently

00:31:50.400 --> 00:31:52.540
play with. Yes. Whenever there's a Zapper game.

00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:53.820
And, yeah, we...

00:31:53.820 --> 00:31:56.140
I'll be honest, we played for like three hours.

00:31:56.420 --> 00:31:59.160
We were sucked in pretty quickly.

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:02.060
And then we played some Duck Hunt.

00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:03.260
But it's easy.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:07.340
I guess what I mean is, is it easier or harder with two players?

00:32:07.360 --> 00:32:09.820
It's the same. It's just kind of like alternating between.

00:32:10.080 --> 00:32:11.360
And then like one of you dies, you're out.

00:32:11.420 --> 00:32:12.440
Oh. It doesn't...

00:32:12.440 --> 00:32:14.300
I see. Yeah, we're not both shooting at the same time.

00:32:14.500 --> 00:32:15.780
I guess that's important to note.

00:32:16.060 --> 00:32:17.100
Yeah, I guess that would have been impossible.

00:32:18.220 --> 00:32:22.980
But... Yeah, it's really just so you don't have to wait for your other person to be completely

00:32:22.980 --> 00:32:24.680
done. You just take turns between levels.

00:32:24.780 --> 00:32:28.180
I'm going to give it a pass because it's an NES game, but I would have appreciated it

00:32:28.180 --> 00:32:29.040
if you could both shoot at the same time.

00:32:29.040 --> 00:32:30.140
That would have definitely been...

00:32:30.140 --> 00:32:32.880
That would have helped it make you feel, too, like, more realistic.

00:32:32.880 --> 00:32:35.640
Yeah, like, you know, you're like two buddy buddies.

00:32:36.020 --> 00:32:38.700
What are buddy cops? Buddy buddies.

00:32:40.220 --> 00:32:41.120
Fighting each other.

00:32:41.640 --> 00:32:42.640
What am I talking about?

00:32:42.740 --> 00:32:43.980
I don't know what you're talking about. It's okay.

00:32:44.280 --> 00:32:45.380
It's okay, Joe. It's fine.

00:32:48.440 --> 00:32:55.140
There is a secret word special offer that Sunsoft was offering throughout the game.

00:32:55.240 --> 00:32:56.380
Does anybody know about this?

00:32:56.520 --> 00:33:00.720
Yes. Yeah. So, the way that it worked was, it's in the manual.

00:33:00.900 --> 00:33:06.000
This is your only way to get the official Freedom Force self-adhesive decals.

00:33:06.220 --> 00:33:07.620
Ha! Okay? Stickers.

00:33:08.020 --> 00:33:09.000
Yeah. Yeah, stickers.

00:33:10.220 --> 00:33:12.020
And it came with an entry form.

00:33:12.200 --> 00:33:15.800
You had to find out the three secret words in the game, write them down, give them your

00:33:15.800 --> 00:33:22.140
name, street address, all that stuff, date of birth, and enclose $1, and then you would

00:33:22.140 --> 00:33:23.080
get the stickers in return.

00:33:23.100 --> 00:33:24.760
You still need to pay? You still need to pay.

00:33:24.880 --> 00:33:26.440
You have to pay. I didn't really need to put a dollar.

00:33:26.440 --> 00:33:28.780
Yeah. It says that in the manual.

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:30.500
It describes it as such, okay?

00:33:30.640 --> 00:33:33.760
It's almost like, I'll get to the joke at the end.

00:33:33.920 --> 00:33:39.060
At the end of the fifth scene of round one, a special secret word will briefly be shown.

00:33:39.300 --> 00:33:42.980
An additional word will appear after rounds two and three.

00:33:43.340 --> 00:33:45.260
In all, there are three secret words.

00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:49.820
Collect all three and write them down on the special order form opposite this page, and

00:33:49.820 --> 00:33:52.980
you will receive the official Freedom Force self-adhesive decal set.

00:33:53.920 --> 00:34:00.540
And those three secret words remind me of that Simpsons episode where they put join the Navy

00:34:00.540 --> 00:34:02.840
backwards as like Eno Nassidano.

00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:04.820
It's like one of the only Simpsons episodes I've ever seen.

00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:10.240
Yeah. And it's like, this was all just actually funded by the military to start like an anti-terrorism

00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:11.440
campaign in 1988.

00:34:12.540 --> 00:34:14.380
But I don't know what the three secret words were.

00:34:14.560 --> 00:34:17.100
I don't think I do. I know what the three secret words were.

00:34:17.100 --> 00:34:23.460
Please, what are they? No, this is only because if you go on, if you Google the manual, if you Google the manual,

00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:27.000
in the manual that has been scanned on, it was someone's-

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:28.320
Oh, somebody filled it out. Somebody filled it out.

00:34:28.500 --> 00:34:30.500
They filled it out, and it's erased.

00:34:30.760 --> 00:34:31.840
Oh my goodness, I saw it.

00:34:31.880 --> 00:34:35.560
The three words are poop, pee with one E, and butt.

00:34:35.860 --> 00:34:37.540
With one T. And it's like tried to be erased.

00:34:37.720 --> 00:34:40.220
Yeah, butt with one T. It's like tried to be erased.

00:34:40.420 --> 00:34:41.900
Those are clearly not secret words.

00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:44.400
Obviously. But I think it's funny that we all have that copy.

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:46.120
It's so funny that it's P-E, too.

00:34:46.260 --> 00:34:47.400
That cracks me up.

00:34:48.040 --> 00:34:50.160
I think the butt only has one T as well.

00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:51.660
Yeah, you're right. Poop.

00:34:52.580 --> 00:34:55.360
I'm trying to find the-

00:34:55.360 --> 00:34:57.500
If you find them, I'm going to mail them in.

00:34:57.500 --> 00:34:58.700
Yeah. Get my piece of the cows.

00:34:59.380 --> 00:35:03.260
Unfortunately, there is another game called Freedom Force, so it's not that.

00:35:04.840 --> 00:35:08.040
Apparently, there's a level select option here for cheats.

00:35:08.880 --> 00:35:10.740
I mean, I know that I saw one of them.

00:35:10.780 --> 00:35:16.040
I can't remember it. I was watching a long play after playing it like a week prior.

00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:19.120
And what's it?

00:35:19.120 --> 00:35:23.760
Like, yeah, they are out there if you just watch the YouTube videos.

00:35:24.220 --> 00:35:26.820
Got it. There's a couple of things here.

00:35:26.940 --> 00:35:29.780
These are all unverified, so believe them at your own will.

00:35:30.080 --> 00:35:32.380
But there's a level select cheat.

00:35:32.400 --> 00:35:33.620
You pause the game.

00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:38.900
Then you press the A button 16 times and for one more time for each level.

00:35:38.900 --> 00:35:45.100
For example, you must press A on first level 17 times and 21 times for the fifth level.

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:47.440
This only works for the first run of the game.

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:51.780
So in order to level select the first level, you have to hit it that many times?

00:35:51.900 --> 00:35:52.820
Yes, but 17 times.

00:35:52.820 --> 00:35:54.180
Or just not hit it at all?

00:35:54.540 --> 00:35:56.260
For the first level? Well, yeah, for the first level.

00:35:56.400 --> 00:36:01.240
But I guess if you wanted to go back, you know, because if you're on the first run and you're

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:02.600
on stage three, you can do that.

00:36:03.060 --> 00:36:07.160
Okay. Then for the sound test, all right, this would be very useful if it's true.

00:36:09.220 --> 00:36:12.700
You unplug the zapper and plug the second controller in.

00:36:12.700 --> 00:36:19.460
Now, on the player selection screen, press and hold left, up, B, and A on controller 2.

00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:22.420
If done right, the sound test should appear.

00:36:22.720 --> 00:36:24.780
Press A and B together to quit the sound test.

00:36:25.080 --> 00:36:26.060
I'm pretty involved.

00:36:27.080 --> 00:36:32.260
After beating the game three times, when the word congratulations appears, press A on the

00:36:32.260 --> 00:36:34.620
second controller and a hidden message will appear.

00:36:34.940 --> 00:36:36.360
Do we know what the hidden message is?

00:36:36.440 --> 00:36:38.100
We don't. Okay. I don't believe any of these.

00:36:38.320 --> 00:36:42.300
This is like press A 1,000 times and you'll fight Goku.

00:36:42.700 --> 00:36:44.300
Super Smash Bros. 64, you know?

00:36:45.660 --> 00:36:50.700
And then beat the game up to four times in a row to see each time a different short ending

00:36:50.700 --> 00:36:53.920
message. It also varies if you reach the end with the second player.

00:36:54.320 --> 00:36:57.160
Ooh. So that's interesting to know.

00:36:57.360 --> 00:36:58.520
We don't know if these are true or not.

00:36:58.600 --> 00:37:08.300
Can't confirm them. Does anybody have any other stray thoughts on Freedom Force?

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:15.080
Just one. I think that items should be in the game and not in the heads up display, personally.

00:37:15.540 --> 00:37:16.340
That's a good idea.

00:37:16.640 --> 00:37:18.400
Yeah. It's a lot easier to spot.

00:37:19.360 --> 00:37:22.540
Where would you like them to fall, though?

00:37:24.300 --> 00:37:26.260
I don't know. Like in the field of play.

00:37:26.580 --> 00:37:27.620
Yeah. In the field of play.

00:37:27.620 --> 00:37:30.180
In doorways. Maybe like dropping from parachutes or something.

00:37:30.540 --> 00:37:34.320
Because I'd just be worried about like, you know, with the hitboxes that like you go

00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:37.140
to shoot the gun and instead you shoot the person.

00:37:37.420 --> 00:37:40.640
You know, like where would it be? They would have to make sure it's always programmed so it wouldn't fall where an enemy is.

00:37:40.640 --> 00:37:43.220
Right. I would say that they would be placed, not falling.

00:37:43.480 --> 00:37:45.440
Or that, yeah. I like that.

00:37:45.540 --> 00:37:48.480
But I did actually really like the way it played in the game.

00:37:48.620 --> 00:37:49.620
Even though you couldn't do it.

00:37:49.880 --> 00:37:50.720
Well, I couldn't get the health.

00:37:51.200 --> 00:37:52.540
But like, yeah, it should be hard to get the health.

00:37:52.540 --> 00:37:54.120
You couldn't get the health, though, because it just went too fast.

00:37:54.120 --> 00:37:56.320
Did you get the health? I did not get the health.

00:37:56.480 --> 00:37:58.040
You couldn't get it because it went too fast, though, right?

00:37:58.140 --> 00:38:01.080
You didn't have a problem with like picking up guns and stuff like that, right?

00:38:01.080 --> 00:38:02.360
Yeah, because it went too fast.

00:38:02.500 --> 00:38:05.820
Just because like I'm sure if I played longer and got better at it, I could maybe get the

00:38:05.820 --> 00:38:09.560
health. I liked how distinctively far away it was from the action field.

00:38:09.720 --> 00:38:12.480
So this way you could just like shoot off, get your thing, go back to the stage.

00:38:12.480 --> 00:38:13.320
Yeah, and it was different, too.

00:38:13.400 --> 00:38:16.160
It was just like a different mechanic that I just thought was interesting, you know?

00:38:17.060 --> 00:38:21.140
Yep. And Freedom Force did get one other release.

00:38:21.140 --> 00:38:24.780
I won't count those as like sequels and spinoffs because it's not really.

00:38:24.940 --> 00:38:28.240
It's just Verse Freedom Force, part of Nintendo's Verse system.

00:38:28.380 --> 00:38:29.360
So it went to arcades.

00:38:29.580 --> 00:38:33.280
And that's pretty cool because then you could play it with like a probably better light gun

00:38:33.280 --> 00:38:37.060
technology. There's no difference, though, in anything about the game.

00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:38.860
So, okay. Not a sequel.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:41.100
Just Verse Freedom Force.

00:38:41.180 --> 00:38:42.300
We've seen this a couple times. Yeah.

00:38:42.300 --> 00:38:43.420
Oh, you mean the Verse.

00:38:43.500 --> 00:38:45.600
But other times the Verse games have been different.

00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:49.780
Verse Ice Climber was like one where you can choose between like eight worlds and stuff.

00:38:49.780 --> 00:38:53.240
And Verse Excitebike had some things going on.

00:38:53.580 --> 00:38:55.120
So this is a half-assed Verse.

00:38:55.200 --> 00:38:57.280
Verse Super Mario Brothers is a completely different game.

00:38:57.360 --> 00:38:58.640
Yeah, it's true. It's very cool.

00:38:59.180 --> 00:39:02.600
I think it's time for the Essential Games List.

00:39:05.320 --> 00:39:07.160
Sam, we'd love to hear your thoughts.

00:39:07.360 --> 00:39:08.800
Please give them. Wow, thank you.

00:39:09.100 --> 00:39:10.380
So these are my thoughts.

00:39:10.600 --> 00:39:13.780
I think that this is one of the better Zapper games.

00:39:13.780 --> 00:39:19.760
I don't think it's as good as Duck Hunt, but I think it's fun and it accomplishes what

00:39:19.760 --> 00:39:24.820
it sets out to do, which I feel like a lot of NES games don't, especially with the Zapper.

00:39:25.060 --> 00:39:26.000
It can get kind of tricky.

00:39:26.960 --> 00:39:35.320
And I think it's solid, but it is what it is, and I don't think it's anything special at

00:39:35.320 --> 00:39:42.540
the same time. So I think if you are a Zapper fan, this is a must-have, but overall, not Essential.

00:39:46.980 --> 00:39:52.300
Hi. I'm Sean, and this is my Essential Games List vote.

00:39:54.180 --> 00:39:55.780
I was just trying to change it up.

00:39:57.360 --> 00:40:03.600
I edit the end of the episode, so when I hear like Sam, Sean, Joe, I think it's like everybody

00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:06.060
knows who you guys are. You might as well just talk one into another.

00:40:06.100 --> 00:40:07.780
You're right. I don't need you to tell me what to do.

00:40:07.780 --> 00:40:08.640
But now it's been established.

00:40:08.760 --> 00:40:09.940
This is good. Okay, good.

00:40:11.340 --> 00:40:15.580
So for, you know, this game, I liked the aesthetic.

00:40:16.380 --> 00:40:21.400
It actually has an interesting sense of humor that we didn't really touch upon.

00:40:21.840 --> 00:40:26.640
They'll show what the new enemy is throughout the game, and they'll show you the reason why

00:40:26.640 --> 00:40:31.780
they're doing it, and one of them is just to get on TV, which is dark in a funny way.

00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:40.420
So, yeah, a lot of the dressings I liked, but I stand by my statement from the beginning

00:40:40.420 --> 00:40:46.640
of the episode that this genre has kind of run its course with the current technology.

00:40:47.460 --> 00:40:50.260
They're all just shooting galleries of one form or another.

00:40:50.940 --> 00:40:53.000
They're not really innovating in any way.

00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:59.780
So while it is fun, and if it existed in a vacuum and there were no other Zapper games,

00:40:59.900 --> 00:41:03.940
this would be just, you know, this would be one of the, this would be a lot of fun.

00:41:05.040 --> 00:41:05.840
It's not essential.

00:41:06.020 --> 00:41:07.000
It's not essential at all.

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:11.280
When I first started looking into this game, I didn't have, I didn't have access to the

00:41:11.280 --> 00:41:13.760
Zapper, so I was just watching a video, and I thought, yeah, that looks kind of cool.

00:41:14.340 --> 00:41:19.020
But I will say, when I played it with the Zapper, I really, it's definitely not Duck Hunt,

00:41:19.140 --> 00:41:21.120
but I really, really love this game.

00:41:22.480 --> 00:41:23.800
And I talked about it a lot with Mark.

00:41:23.920 --> 00:41:25.820
We were talking about, like, should I vote this essential?

00:41:26.060 --> 00:41:32.780
And what we were saying was, this is something, if you feel like sitting down and having a goal

00:41:32.780 --> 00:41:38.100
and having a, like, an end goal in a game where you're trying to beat the game, this is a cool experience.

00:41:38.100 --> 00:41:43.720
So I think what Duck Hunt still has over this is that it's just, it's just, like, kind of pure fun.

00:41:43.840 --> 00:41:46.400
You just sit down, you just play, you're just trying to see how high your score is.

00:41:46.520 --> 00:41:54.080
You can do better than your buddies. But I think that this is, like, so, so slightly below it that I do want to vote it essential.

00:41:54.220 --> 00:41:55.660
I kind of had a feeling that I would be the only one.

00:41:55.660 --> 00:42:01.660
I know I'm, like, usually higher on the Zapper games, but I just think there was a, there was a huge level of polish.

00:42:01.860 --> 00:42:03.160
It was more accurate.

00:42:03.320 --> 00:42:06.740
It was, it's definitely my second favorite Zapper game, and I think, I think everyone should play it.

00:42:06.740 --> 00:42:08.660
I think it's, you can't have a bad time with this game.

00:42:11.780 --> 00:42:18.280
Um, this is my poker face, and I'm going to reveal that I think that this is the best Zapper game we've played.

00:42:18.500 --> 00:42:26.600
And I think it is better than Duck Hunt, and I think that in terms of everything that has been offered in the other Zapper games,

00:42:26.700 --> 00:42:29.640
we were talking, like, oh, you know, like, Gumshoe should have learned lessons,

00:42:29.720 --> 00:42:31.800
and this would have been really cool if it did it this way.

00:42:31.800 --> 00:42:37.640
Instead, I feel like this is the idea of, like, when we were joking around about, like, Hogan's Alley being a minigame

00:42:37.640 --> 00:42:42.020
and Wild Gunman being a minigame, and it's like, oh, if only those could have been, like, full, realized games.

00:42:42.460 --> 00:42:44.500
This is Hogan's Alley as, like, a complete game.

00:42:44.580 --> 00:42:48.180
This actually makes me think, like, Hogan's Alley was just, like, a test run for something,

00:42:48.320 --> 00:42:50.060
for somebody to make something like this.

00:42:50.060 --> 00:42:58.320
And I think that if this game wasn't, like, as hard as I thought it was, like, if reaction times were a little more fair,

00:42:58.520 --> 00:43:02.960
this would have been one of the most fun games I've played on the NES since Balloon Fight.

00:43:03.400 --> 00:43:08.480
You know, it's just, it's very easy because, you know, you don't have to, you don't have a controller,

00:43:08.540 --> 00:43:10.000
you don't have to worry about a bunch of different things.

00:43:10.160 --> 00:43:11.740
You're not in control of when it moves.

00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:21.180
That's a stretch.

00:43:22.040 --> 00:43:26.860
I'm just saying, like, through the, yeah, through, like, going through the airport, going to various different places.

00:43:27.080 --> 00:43:33.280
I think that's what puts it above Duck Hunt for me, is that, like, in Duck Hunt, all you're doing is shooting these ducks,

00:43:33.440 --> 00:43:36.720
and they get a little bit faster, but they do reach a peak momentum.

00:43:36.920 --> 00:43:40.800
In this game, it's more like there's a reason to be doing all this.

00:43:40.800 --> 00:43:42.740
It's a counterterrorism point.

00:43:42.900 --> 00:43:52.560
But also, the, just the way that it handles the UI and the enemies on screen and stuff like that,

00:43:52.700 --> 00:43:54.920
I like what it chose to leave in and leave out.

00:43:54.940 --> 00:43:59.340
I did have some complaints about, like, how the health bar is represented and stuff like that.

00:43:59.840 --> 00:44:06.000
But I think as a complete game, this is the first Zapper game that didn't feel like it had any gimmicks to me

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:10.440
and was more like, other than the bonus game, maybe, but that was like, take it or leave it.

00:44:10.440 --> 00:44:14.920
But I didn't think of that as part of the, part of, like, what might make it essential or not.

00:44:15.220 --> 00:44:17.540
So I think, for me, this is a great game.

00:44:17.980 --> 00:44:20.120
I'm still not going to put it on the essential games list, though.

00:44:20.380 --> 00:44:24.780
And I think that's just because, you know, like, I don't think Zapper games can be essential.

00:44:24.780 --> 00:44:25.840
But you put Duck Hunt on there, right?

00:44:25.840 --> 00:44:29.000
I did, but I think that was more, like, on hype than we were on, like, episode four.

00:44:29.760 --> 00:44:34.060
I don't know if I'd still, like, I don't have Duck Hunt in my top ten games for what it's worth on the NES.

00:44:34.140 --> 00:44:35.380
I think it's still my, like, number three.

00:44:35.380 --> 00:44:36.340
Yeah, but it's fine.

00:44:36.440 --> 00:44:37.280
I'm saying, like, we like that.

00:44:37.460 --> 00:44:41.960
I think, like, I need something better than an NES Zapper in this day and age.

00:44:42.180 --> 00:44:47.880
Like, that must have been revolutionary to play games like Duck Hunt and Freedom Force, like, in 1988.

00:44:48.300 --> 00:45:01.060
But to do it now, it's definitely like, well, I've been to the arcade, and let me tell you, like, when you play, you know, like, Time Crisis 4, it's like, wow, that's a fun game to play.

00:45:01.060 --> 00:45:11.600
Right. But I definitely think, like, Freedom Force hits that right balance of, like, arcade fun, Zapper fun, and a reason to take it home, too.

00:45:11.740 --> 00:45:24.280
Because you want to continue to play it through because you're not, you know, it's kind of like when I was growing up, I did buy Time Crisis 3 for PlayStation 2 with, like, two Zappers and two gun, light guns.

00:45:24.280 --> 00:45:30.600
Because I wanted to actually, like, see what happens in those games without giving it, like, a billion quarters, you know?

00:45:30.800 --> 00:45:37.300
I wanted to see, like, just a version where you can always continue and just play through things, and that's kind of what it offers in a weird way.

00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:42.380
So I think it's a great game, best Zapper game I've ever played, but it's not going on the Essential Games list.

00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:44.140
Can I add something to mine?

00:45:44.220 --> 00:45:46.840
I forgot to mention something that really stuck out to me.

00:45:46.840 --> 00:45:55.700
So at least the way that I see the, like, the big three Zapper games that we had at the beginning is that Duck Hunt really focuses a lot on aim.

00:45:55.900 --> 00:45:57.640
You know, your precision and your aim.

00:45:58.040 --> 00:46:03.700
Wild Gunman was, like, so much more about your reaction time, and Hogan's Alley was about, like, quick decision making.

00:46:03.880 --> 00:46:05.360
Like, your aim was, it was easy to aim at them.

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:09.960
And I think this kind of hit, like, a balance of all three of those things.

00:46:10.120 --> 00:46:12.880
I mean, you do feel like you can miss these.

00:46:13.000 --> 00:46:14.440
Like, they're small enough that you can miss.

00:46:14.440 --> 00:46:17.300
You know, you do have to aim, like, well.

00:46:17.560 --> 00:46:21.640
And then you have to have quick decision making because there are people that look like the enemies,

00:46:21.660 --> 00:46:23.700
and there are people that, you know, are innocent that you don't want to shoot.

00:46:23.860 --> 00:46:26.260
And it's easy to kind of slip up and miss those.

00:46:26.380 --> 00:46:30.700
And then you have to have the reaction time for the ammo and things that come down at the bottom, you know.

00:46:30.840 --> 00:46:33.060
I think that Gotcha had all that, too, though.

00:46:33.280 --> 00:46:38.780
I mean, maybe not false positives and, like, that there are people you shouldn't kill,

00:46:38.820 --> 00:46:41.820
but you had to prioritize who you were going to shoot.

00:46:41.820 --> 00:46:45.700
But it was just based on who popped up first because they all had the same reaction time.

00:46:45.820 --> 00:46:47.140
Nobody was shooting, like, faster.

00:46:47.400 --> 00:46:51.840
Yeah, and I think overall Gotcha was just, like, regardless of these elements I'm talking about,

00:46:51.880 --> 00:46:56.100
it was, like, a more shallow experience to me just, like, because it just seemed, like,

00:46:56.180 --> 00:46:58.640
something about it seemed, like, easier.

00:46:58.840 --> 00:47:00.780
The moving seemed a little more arbitrary.

00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:02.220
It was just kind of go to the left, go to the right.

00:47:02.240 --> 00:47:04.740
It was, like, it was almost, like, easy to break.

00:47:05.320 --> 00:47:07.040
Okay. Where I shouldn't say break.

00:47:07.160 --> 00:47:13.880
Like, it wasn't broken. It was also just a much slower game in general, and I think that the added use of the controller hurt it.

00:47:14.120 --> 00:47:18.300
Yeah, and I think there were different difficulty levels, but I think that there was one where you could just run

00:47:18.660 --> 00:47:20.900
and, like, nobody would be able to get a shot off at you.

00:47:22.680 --> 00:47:24.180
But, yeah, that was just, like, another big thing.

00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:27.840
Because I was trying to put my finger on what I liked so much about this game, but that's it.

00:47:28.840 --> 00:47:29.680
All right, cool.

